      "message": "I have several problems with this change.\n\n1. There is no bugreport. The problem should be described there in details, including steps to reproduce.\n2. I don\u0027t understand what exactly fails with your custom identity backend. Why do you think that your behavior is correct, and the existing in keystone is incorrect? From the code i see that there is expectation to have `password_expires_at` and `options` - why can\u0027t the custom backend provide those?\n3. The commit message writes about KeyError due to non-existing shadow user, but i don\u0027t see anything related to shadow users in the code. Is the commit message up to date?",
